  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Consider three boxes, each containing <math><mn>10</mn></math> balls labelled <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>10</mn></math>. Suppose one ball is randomly drawn from each of the boxes. Denote by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math>, the label of the ball drawn from the <math><msup><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow></msup></math> box, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Then, the number of ways in which the balls can be chosen such that <math><msub><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> is :",
    "image": null
  },
